pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
>Except that Psi Bolt -- in my experience -- sucks.  I've never taken
>serious damage to that.

Before Rodney starts escalating due to being killed, his Psi Bolts do
15-90 damage, divided by two (round up) if you have either of HSPDAM
or MR, and divided by two twice (round up each time) if you have both.
Thus, with both MR and HSPDAM, you take 4-23 damage; with only one,
you take 8-45.  No further reduction is achieved by having negative
AC.

The melee attacks you gave him will each do an average of 24 damage,
subject to further reduction by HPHDAM and negative AC.  Assuming AC
-25 and no HPHDAM, each attack will average 11 damage, yielding 22.
HPHDAM halves the damage of each attack *after* armour is taken into
account, so with AC -25 and HPHDAM, each attack will average 6 damage,
yielding 12.

The melee attacks can really punish people with mediocre AC, of course.
On the other hand, the melee attacks won't get any better (other than
hitting more often) as Rodney gains levels; the spells *will* (though
admittedly not by much).  On the gripping hand, HSPDAM (both Orbs of
Weight, the PYEC, and the Eye of the Aethiopica) is more common than
HPHDAM (Orb of Fate and Master Key of Thievery), and characters who
remain Lawful for the entire duration of the game can't get HPHDAM at
all unless they're Valkyries. (Flipside to that: faithful Chaotics
can't get HSPDAM unless they're Wizards.)

Of course, you could have just slapped some extra damage dice into
Rodney's spellcasting attack in the same way that Orcus gets an extra
eight dice :-)
